--
__remove_cv, __remove_reference and __remove_cvref (and
__is_nothrow_convertible, __is_pointer_interconvertible_base_of) are
scanned as builtins when followed by '(' -- regardless of the HOST gcc's
version, which used to gate them (gcc >= 13): a preprocessed translation
unit from a newer gcc failed on a gcc-11 host (gcc16_optional_transform on
the 22.04 CI runners).  Sibling cpp11_revertible_builtin_remove_cv_alias
covers libstdc++ 11's alias templates of the same names.
Also: __remove_cvref(const int &) stripped the cv-qualifiers BEFORE the
reference (leaving `const int'); N5008 [meta.trans.other]/3 defines it as
remove_cv_t<remove_reference_t<T>>.
